{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/160591-converting-dread-powers-to-supernatural-merits-gmc","id":160591,"title":"Converting Dread Powers to Supernatural Merits? [GMC]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-05T22:28:41-07:00","id":160591,"title":"Converting Dread Powers to Supernatural Merits? [GMC]","content":"Just like the title says; Mortal Remains pegs Dread Powers as 2XP/Dot. Now, I'm planning on running a Stigmatic game this summer, and I want to expand the offering of Supernatural merits, but I kinda don't want to hand out Endowments (Anthropophagy would otherwise solve my issue.)<br /> <br /> Any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T00:12:18-07:00","id":160623,"title":"","content":"You just want to be careful which ones you convert. Dread Powers tend to be pretty powerful.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, let them buy Dread Powers as Dread Powers, according them some special, weird status. For instance, in a planned Demon: The Descent game, I planned on giving one of my players who wants to play a Stigmatic the opportunity to buy Biomechanical Nightmare and Ghost in the Machine, saying they've become some stranger, more powerful kind of Stigmatic as the result of weird God-Machine experimentation.<br /> <br /> If you're not having any other splats and you're unafraid of them being powerful, you could give them the more martial ones. Honestly since they're Stigmatics, I'd stick to techgnostic-like powers and flavoring the other ones if you plan to use them. I suggest creating a list of which ones are approved and which aren't, so players can know which ones they can buy.<br /> <br /> One limitation I might suggest is only converting those Dread Powers which cost 1 WP.<br /> <br /> Fluid Lessons strikes me as one that could be cool. Eye for Desire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T01:21:14-07:00","id":160646,"title":"","content":"Converting dread powers, the generic abilities of monsters, into supernatural merits, the abilities only vanilla mortals (and some noted exceptions) can acquire seems like an odd thing to do.<br /> <br /> However, I think you're looking at it the wrong way.<br /> <br /> Dread powers are the generic powers of monsters, ranging from slashers to spirits, so you don't actually need an excuse to make dread powers available, their very premise is that they are available.<br /> <br /> Now the default position is certainly &quot;dread powers&quot; instead of their own unique abilities, but that really depends on ST whim. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T03:52:26-07:00","id":160708,"title":"","content":"My plan was more to use them as a guideline to make more concrete supernatural merits than to allow full Dread Power access; more like basing a merit off Ghost in the Machine than making a merit that lets people use Ghost in the Machine, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> In any case, I <i>just</i> remembered R&amp;D. Hunter, is there anything you <i>can't</i> help with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T02:34:07-07:00","id":161513,"title":"","content":"Oh so you just remembered the bit where even hunters can score dread powers as endowments bit?<br /> <br /> Hmm, actually that whole R&amp;D mechanic would be an interesting mechanic for stigmatics. Reading strange texts that flow from language to language, arranging for a procedure by some strange group or creature, fiddling with devices that no one on earth understands, man that sounds very appropriate for a god-machine game.<br /> <br /> And lol, don't try to give me a big head, I just like to buy WW products and peruse them repeatedly, since I haven't actually played in freaking forever I can at least help out occasionally here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:45:34-07:00","id":161932,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly trying to see if I can get some quick merits that the Players can take to supplement the ones already in the book; buying <i>actual</i> Dark Powers comes later, and will totally follow R&amp;D mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T23:23:57-07:00","id":162257,"title":"","content":"Hmm well you mentioned you don't want them to use endowments, but how about expand their abilities by giving them access to plug-ins?<br /> <br /> So say they're brains are rewired ala Dollhouse? <br /> <br /> Or if that doesn't work for you, how about allowing them to gain the gifted merit from Witchhunters? I mean a merit that enables a muggle to have supernatural powers, that pretty much sounds like a supernatural merit to me. The only difference is technically they aren't mortal only, although I believe the writer said that was sort of intended on the old forum. <br /> <br /> Although some of the mysteries the gifted can mimic might be too much for you're preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}